LME changes: local/theme paths, optional source texture, Theme knobs scaling
rim/blur/edge width over the upstream production wiring (frost 2.2,
rim 0.45, bezel 3..14 x 0.28, thickness bezel x 0.8). Edge/border optics
are restored to upstream liquid_glass.frag exactly: finite-difference edge
gradient, Fresnel env reflection, inner shadow, broad spec, meniscus,
fringe, lens zoom with lensK, blurLod/blurredAt 0.9 falloff, GRAIN 0.004.
Single infra exception: the backdrop is the wallpaper snapshot Image via
GlassState rather than upstream's live WallpaperBlur texture. When no
snapshot is ready the colour base is vec3(0.32,0.34,0.38) and the
dispersion/Fresnel fetches are skipped; with a ready snapshot the upstream
pipeline runs unchanged. Pointer coordinates follow LME's existing spring
engine; no extra render layers are added. The real application backdrop
remains compositor-owned; no live desktop capture is performed. The
surrounding lifecycle/neutral-theme integration is LME code.

Glass-on-glass nesting (Liquid Glass 2.0 G1): LME wires the walk into its own
GlassMaterial host. The level counts marked ancestor strata (GlassMaterial and
GlassPanel carry upstream's isGlassFill marker); the walk skips the carrier
(the child of a stratum that contains the walker), so a marked glass container
counts through its own embedded layer, never as itself. The level recomputes
only on tree events: parent/backdrop changes and childrenChanged on watched
ancestors, coalesced with Qt.callLater and bounded to 48 levels. Without a
backdrop the domain stops at the host window's content item. Nested optics
follow upstream GlassFill.qml: rim and frost attenuation at the material
level, with nest passed into the renderer whose uniform already softens bevel,
veil, bulge and grain. Upstream does not re-walk on allowed changes; LME
matches that.

Liquid-glass renderer refinements (#87-#91, LME, modifying the adapted files
above): the lens shader (liquid-glass.frag, rebuilt .qsb) gained a
compositor-blur yield path (transparent base with bounded tint/alpha when true
backdrop is applied, niri >= 26.04 and a blur region is active), adaptive
contrast (luminance-compensated bounded tint) with a tunable grain uniform, and
a contrast-floor alpha clamp (yield/normal caps) — all LME changes layered on
the restored upstream optics; backdrop sampling and lifecycle remain LME-owned.

